{"author":"Rebar Bot","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"## Census: per-nodeid attribution\n\nThe acceptance criteria reference this enumeration. Every one of the 51 sandbox failures is named here and assigned to exactly one cause, so verification checks named tests rather than inferring a cause from a residual count. The partition sums to 51 with no test in two buckets and none unassigned.\n\n### Owned by this ticket — git identity (20)\n\n```\ntests/unit/test_identity_4e9d_heldout.py::test_append_event_composer_stamps_email\ntests/unit/test_identity_4e9d_heldout.py::test_compact_snapshot_composer_stamps_email\ntests/unit/test_identity_4e9d_heldout.py::test_per_entry_comment_attribution\ntests/unit/test_identity_4e9d_heldout.py::test_rebuild_snapshot_composer_stamps_email\ntests/unit/test_identity_4e9d_heldout.py::test_reduced_state_surfaces_author_id_top_level\ntests/unit/test_identity_4e9d.py::test_author_id_present_when_identity_set\ntests/unit/test_identity_4e9d.py::test_create_event_carries_author_email\ntests/unit/test_identity_ddbe.py::test_resolve_current_identity_git_email_default\ntests/unit/test_commit_and_push_tickets_branch_heldout.py::test_supplied_and_ambient_identity_do_not_mutate_git_config\ntests/unit/test_reviewbot_ensure_tickets.py::test_ensure_makes_clone_writable_and_durable\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_inbound_signing_9e76.py::test_inbound_write_stamps_and_signs_as_identity\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_inbound_signing_9e76.py::test_inbound_write_unsigned_without_key\ntests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py::test_pause_and_resume_dispatch_happy_path\ntests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py::test_pause_and_resume_real_cli_subprocess_round_trip\ntests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_cli_heldout.py::test_pause_refuses_blank_reason_and_missing_git_email_without_write\ntests/interfaces/facades/test_bridge_programmatic_e2e_heldout.py::test_pause_and_resume_share_the_durable_control_ref_across_surfaces\ntests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py::test_missing_git_email_aborts_before_pause_or_mutation[doctor]\ntests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py::test_missing_git_email_aborts_before_pause_or_mutation[fsck]\ntests/scripts/graph/test_repair_pause_ownership.py::test_doctor_repair_owns_same_pause_contract_and_clears_it\ntests/scripts/graph/test_repair_pause_ownership.py::test_fsck_repair_owns_pause_during_mutation_and_clears_it\n```\n\nNote how many of these concern **missing git email** specifically. That is the signature of the injected command-scope config outranking what the fixtures set, and it is the same condition `scrub_ambient_git_config()` was already written to defeat in the bridge tests.\n\n### Owned by this ticket — semgrep (8)\n\n```\ntests/unit/grounding/test_engine_b.py::test_builtin_smell_matches_via_real_engine\ntests/unit/grounding/test_engine_b.py::test_invalid_detector_is_quarantined_and_does_not_abort_scan\ntests/unit/grounding/test_engine_b.py::test_non_relative_paths_glob_is_quarantined_not_a_crash\ntests/unit/grounding/test_conformance.py::test_opengrep_timeout_via_harness\ntests/unit/test_code_review_public_exposure.py::test_positive_public_exposure_matches\ntests/unit/test_code_review_public_exposure.py::test_public_exposure_match_stays_advisory\ntests/unit/test_code_review_conflict_markers.py::test_positive_conflict_markers_match\ntests/unit/test_code_review_conflict_markers.py::test_conflict_marker_match_stays_advisory\n```\n\n### Owned by this ticket — `ps` (1)\n\n```\ntests/scripts/test_check_orphaned_load.py::test_real_adapter_reads_live_process_table_without_raising\n```\n\n### Not this ticket — pandoc (17), `dc28-2807-5b1d-4da7`\n\n```\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_pypandoc_and_pandoc_versions_are_pinned\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_pandoc_emits_no_color_form\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_dc_box_table_is_wrapped_verbatim\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_dc_code_arrows_are_never_rewritten\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_dc_heading_has_no_content_free_anchor\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_dc_preservation_failure_returns_exact_unit\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_dc_segmenting_passthrough\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_dc_table_wrapped_once_in_noformat\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_real_jira_writer_output_shapes[# Heading\\n-h1. {anchor:}Heading\\n]\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_real_jira_writer_output_shapes[**b**\\n-*b*\\n]\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_real_jira_writer_output_shapes[*i*\\n-_i_\\n]\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_real_jira_writer_output_shapes[`mono`\\n-{{mono}}\\n]\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_wiki_render.py::test_real_jira_writer_output_shapes[[l](http://x)\\n-[l|http://x]\\n]\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_cutover.py::test_dc_backend_create_path_renders_like_the_update_path\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_cutover.py::test_dc_create_path_renders_like_the_update_path\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/test_rich_text_cutover.py::test_dc_cutover_sends_rendered_wiki\ntests/unit/rebar_reconciler/diffing/test_diff_comments_cutover_neutral.py::test_the_rendered_form_really_does_differ\n```\n\nAll 13 in `test_wiki_render.py` are the module that documents \"a silently absent or drifted pandoc must FAIL, not skip\" — which is why this bucket was split out rather than remedied by a skip.\n\n### Not this ticket — SemLock (4), `0eba-cfd8-34b0-4cb7`\n\n```\ntests/unit/test_marker_fcntl_guard.py::test_marker_lock_serializes_posix_access\ntests/unit/test_network_guard_local_ipc.py::test_network_guard_allows_forkserver_multiprocessing\ntests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_atomic_completion_close.py::test_two_processes_publish_at_most_one_equivalent_same_ticket_bundle\ntests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py::test_a_contended_fcntl_leg_reads_as_held\n```\n\n### Not this ticket — close gate (1), `9753-647b-2f85-40ef`\n\n```\ntests/interfaces/lifecycle/test_completion_gate.py::test_file_impact_close_fetches_before_rejecting_stale_clone\n```\n\n### Arithmetic\n\n20 + 8 + 1 + 17 + 4 + 1 = **51**.\n\nSource: `make test` under the agent sandbox against unmodified `origin/main`, in a throwaway worktree. Reproduced with identical membership across repeated runs — the set is stable, not sampled."},"env_id":"eea68b7f-6697-488b-ac52-744e2ed8e96f","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1789693246873016531,"uuid":"ef4acdbf-b100-4ebd-b958-80b8e2406410"}